     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee rrttwwnn
           ddeevviiccee rrttwwnnffww
           ddeevviiccee rrttwwnn__uussbb
           ddeevviiccee rrttwwnn__ppccii
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann
           ddeevviiccee ffiirrmmwwaarree

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place follow‐
     ing lines in loader.conf(5):

           if_rtwn_pci_load="YES"
           if_rtwn_usb_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrttwwnn driver provides support for 802.11n/ac wireless network PHYs
     supplied by rtwn_pci(4) and rtwn_usb(4).

     The rrttwwnn driver supports ssttaattiioonn, aaddhhoocc, hhoossttaapp and mmoonniittoorr mode opera‐
     tion.  There are no limitations for number of mmoonniittoorr mode virtual inter‐
     faces; in addition to any other virtual interface one ssttaattiioonn interface
     can be added (Note: RTL8821AU supports two non-monitor mode interfaces at
     the same time).

     All chips have hardware support for WEP, AES-CCM and TKIP encryption.

     The rrttwwnn driver can be configured at runtime with ifconfig(8).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The rrttwwnn driver supports USB and PCI devices with the following chipsets:

           ••   Realtek 802.11n wireless 8188e (RTL8188E)
           ••   Realtek 802.11n wireless 8192c (RTL8192C)
           ••   Realtek 802.11n wireless 8192e (RTL8192E)
           ••   Realtek 802.11ac wireless 8812a (RTL8812A)
           ••   Realtek 802.11ac wireless 8821a (RTL8821A)

     For specific devices, see rtwn_pci(4) and rtwn_usb(4).

